  "researchNote": "The Utah National Guard's own site (ut.ng.mil) returned an error from this environment and the state veterans site blocked automated requests (403), and no Utah Code provision enumerating National Guard state decorations could be located. Award names come from the unsourced Utah section of Wikipedia's 'List of decorations awarded by the United States National Guard' cross-checked against USA Military Medals (usamm.com) current product listings, which independently confirm 9 of 15 names as real, currently-sold ribbons (Service, Achievement, Recruiting, Emergency Service, Medal of Merit, Commendation, Basic Training, and the 'Cross' and an unlabeled second Achievement-style ribbon believed to correspond to the Deteur Digniory). Several USAMM product descriptions state a relative wear order (e.g. 'Worn after the UT Medal of Merit and before the UT Deteur Digniory ribbon', '2nd highest UTNG award ... below the UT Medal of Valor') but these are the retailer's own descriptive copy, not an official regulation, so they were not used to assign inStatePrecedence. Neither lead is a .mil/.gov/regulation source, so the file and every entry are flagged needs-source.",
